    "bio": "Sudeshna Hanmant Shivankar is an Indian sprinter specializing in relays and individual sprint events. She secured a silver medal in the Women's 100m at the National Open Athletics Championships with a personal best of 11.64s, earning her a spot in India's 4x100m relay preparatory camp for the Asian Games 2026. She also won gold in the 100m at the National Games and was part of the Indian women's 4x100m relay team that clinched gold at the Asian Relays 2026 with a time of 43.85s. Earlier in her career, she achieved a hat-trick in sprints at the Khelo India Youth Games, winning gold in the 100m, 200m, and 4x100m.",
